<details class="panel overview-explanation"><summary>Metric definitions</summary><p>All-time means every registration currently in the restricted data source at the timestamp above. Businesses are unique business IDs; Users are unique nonanonymous Auth IDs. Deleted records are not reconstructed. Stages use the same precedence as Businesses: live public page, saved profile without a page, configured service without a profile, neither service nor profile, or unknown when a fact is unavailable. Individual location and setup facts remain on Businesses.</p><p>These totals share one database snapshot. A later directory page can differ if registrations change. Unavailable or stale responses show an error rather than zero or a healthy status. The known-test list is maintained from controlled test records and may not identify every trial.</p></details>
